<header><p class="st-kicker">city state · Greece and the Aegean</p><h1 class="st-title">Argos</h1><p class="st-meta">900 BCE – 146 BCE (approx.) · capital Argos</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Ancient city of the Argolid, Sparta's enduring rival in the Peloponnese, famed for the sanctuary of Hera and the sculptor Polykleitos.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/argo">Argos</a> lies in the Argive plain below the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/larissa">Larisa</a> and Aspis hills and was inhabited from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bronze-age">Bronze Age</a>. In the early <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iron-age">Iron Age</a> Dorian settlers made it the leading city of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/argolid">Argolid</a>. In the 7th century BCE King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pheidon-of-argos">Pheidon</a>, credited with standard measures, made it the strongest power in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peloponnese">Peloponnese</a>, and Argos beat <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/sparta">Sparta</a> at Hysiai c. 669 BCE.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/argo">Argos</a> controlled the great <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/argive-heraion">Heraion</a> between it and <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-mycenae">Mycenae</a> and was a centre of bronze sculpture, home of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ageladas">Hageladas</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/polykleitos">Polykleitos</a>. Its power was broken when <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cleomenes-i">Cleomenes I</a> of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/sparta">Sparta</a> destroyed its army at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-sepeia">Sepeia</a> c. 494 BCE. Argos stayed neutral in 480 BCE, then destroyed Mycenae and <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-tiryns">Tiryns</a> and adopted democracy.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>Allied with <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/athens">Athens</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/argo">Argos</a> was defeated at <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/mantinea">Mantinea</a> in 418 BCE. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pyrrhus-of-epirus">Pyrrhus</a> of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-epirus">Kingdom of Epirus</a> died fighting in its streets in 272 BCE. Argos joined the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/achaean-league">Achaean League</a> in 229 BCE and passed under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a> in 146 BCE.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="city state, 900 BCE – 146 BCE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M24 82 V42 H32 V34 H40 V42 H46 V34 H54 V42 H60 V34 H68 V42 H76 V82 Z"/><path d="M44 82 V66 Q50 58 56 66 V82"/><path d="M34 54 H40 M60 54 H66"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">city state</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Greece and the Aegean</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:41.79%;width:15.00%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>900 BCE – 146 BCE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/10th-century-bce">10th century BCE</a> – <a href="/centuries/2nd-century-bce">2nd century BCE</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>city state</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>bureaucratic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Argos</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Pheidon</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Greek religion; cult of Hera</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Doric Greek</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/greece">Greece</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Argeia</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=-523&amp;focus=argos" aria-label="Argos on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5247 824 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Argos lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5567 1080L5549 1060M5567 1080L5304 942"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5549 1060h0M5304 942h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5567 1080h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5567 1080h